WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.745 --> 00:00:18.227
After the bullfight, Polynesia and Charles collected the money from Don Enrique.

2
00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:21.368
They found a woman opening up her shop again.

3
00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:23.129
"Quickly, Charles!"

4
00:00:23.629 --> 00:00:24.569
said Polynesia.

5
00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:28.191
"We must buy everything she has and get it to our boat."

6
00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:29.471
"What's the hurry?"

7
00:00:29.972 --> 00:00:30.672
Charles asked.

8
00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:34.057
"Soon the people will be angry at Dr.

9
00:00:34.097 --> 00:00:35.857
Dolittle," she replied.

10
00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:38.198
"He has stopped all bullfights."

11
00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:42.719
Charles carried food and supplies back and forth to the boat.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.180
Soon Tommy came along and helped him.

13
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.741
"Where is the doctor?"

14
00:00:47.101 --> 00:00:47.981
whispered Charles.

15
00:00:48.001 --> 00:00:50.082
"Hiding on the boat.

16
00:00:50.602 --> 00:00:53.443
The people are looking for him," Tommy answered.

17
00:00:54.303 --> 00:00:56.404
An angry mob appeared in the distance.

18
00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:00.149
"Look! That's Dolittle's people!

19
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.430
Get them!"

20
00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:02.971
they yelled.

21
00:01:04.972 --> 00:01:07.413
Charles and Tommy ran as fast as they could.

22
00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.654
"Doctor! Get the boat started!"

23
00:01:10.254 --> 00:01:11.135
shouted Charles.

24
00:01:11.815 --> 00:01:14.216
Dr. Dolittle came out of his hiding place.

25
00:01:14.997 --> 00:01:17.118
He ran to the wheel and started the boat.

26
00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:19.299
Charles and Tommy jumped on.

27
00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.420
They were off to sea again.

28
00:01:24.136 --> 00:01:27.499
The next few weeks were filled with beautiful warm weather.

29
00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:30.801
Tommy was so glad to leave Capa Blanca.

30
00:01:30.821 --> 00:01:34.764
"Will the mayor keep his promise never to have bullfights again?"

31
00:01:35.485 --> 00:01:36.185
Tommy asked.

32
00:01:37.046 --> 00:01:38.907
"Yes," answered the doctor.

33
00:01:38.927 --> 00:01:41.929
"That's why the people were so angry."

34
00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:46.593
"Were you at all afraid of the bulls, Dr.

35
00:01:46.613 --> 00:01:48.474
Dolittle?" asked Charles.

36
00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:50.676
Dr. Dolittle shook his head.

37
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.321
"Animals never hurt others unless they are hurt first," he said.

38
00:01:55.341 --> 00:01:58.022
"They're very different from humans that way."

39
00:01:58.762 --> 00:02:03.083
Then the doctor pulled up his net and shouted loudly, "A fidgit!

40
00:02:03.604 --> 00:02:04.464
I got a fidgit!"

41
00:02:07.005 --> 00:02:08.845
Tommy had never heard of a fidgit.

42
00:02:09.465 --> 00:02:12.026
It looked like a plain little silver fish to him.

43
00:02:12.046 --> 00:02:14.006
"This," Dr.

44
00:02:14.047 --> 00:02:19.088
Dolittle pointed excitedly, "will help me understand the shellfish language."

45
00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:21.216
"Do fidgits speak shellfish?"

46
00:02:21.957 --> 00:02:22.677
asked Tommy.

47
00:02:22.697 --> 00:02:27.878
"No, but they are relatives of gorfins," explained the doctor.

48
00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:31.799
"Gorfins are cousins of the crabs, who speak shellfish!"

49
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.520
Tommy did not understand at all.

50
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.901
Dr. Dolittle worked hard into the night.

51
00:02:38.481 --> 00:02:41.602
Tommy stayed close by in case the doctor needed him.

52
00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:45.223
Finally, the doctor poked his head out of the tank.

53
00:02:46.683 --> 00:02:48.924
"Extraordinary," he remarked.

54
00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:51.569
Tommy rubbed his eyes sleepily.

55
00:02:51.589 --> 00:02:53.311
"What is it, Doctor?"

56
00:02:53.911 --> 00:02:54.451
he asked.

57
00:02:55.872 --> 00:02:57.653
The doctor removed his goggles.

58
00:02:57.674 --> 00:03:02.036
"I want you to listen," he said, "and tell me what you hear."

59
00:03:03.137 --> 00:03:06.619
Tommy put the goggles on and stuck his head into the water.

60
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.543
The tiny fish swam around and around making no sound.

61
00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:14.865
Suddenly Tommy heard a faint noise.

62
00:03:15.485 --> 00:03:17.106
He listened more carefully.

63
00:03:18.187 --> 00:03:21.277
It sounded like: "Don tappan dee gloss."

64
00:03:22.377 --> 00:03:23.718
Tommy pulled his head out.

65
00:03:23.738 --> 00:03:27.900
"Doctor," he gasped, "I think I know what it said."

66
00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.182
"What?" asked Dr.

67
00:03:30.222 --> 00:03:33.143
Dolittle. "Don't tap on the glass!"

68
00:03:33.944 --> 00:03:35.484
Tommy jumped up and down.

69
00:03:35.504 --> 00:03:37.946
"I understood his language!"

70
00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.328
Dr. Dolittle turned pink.

71
00:03:42.348 --> 00:03:49.332
"Um, Tommy," he coughed, "I believe that fidgit is speaking English."

72
00:03:50.044 --> 00:03:51.765
Tommy was very disappointed.

73
00:03:52.425 --> 00:03:54.666
He was never going to learn animal talk.

74
00:03:55.486 --> 00:03:56.147
"But see?

75
00:03:56.667 --> 00:04:03.230
If a fidgit can learn to speak human language, then surely we can speak theirs," the doctor reassured

76
00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.691
him. Dr.

77
00:04:06.751 --> 00:04:08.552
Dolittle pulled out a notepad.

78
00:04:09.512 --> 00:04:12.093
"Here is what I recorded from the fidgit so far."

79
00:04:12.553 --> 00:04:13.594
He began to read.

80
00:04:13.614 --> 00:04:15.335
"'Very rare.

81
00:04:16.015 --> 00:04:16.955
Do not smoke.

82
00:04:17.535 --> 00:04:18.516
Please be quiet.

83
00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:21.466
Don't tap on the glass.'"

84
00:04:21.506 --> 00:04:23.147
Dr. Dolittle scratched his head.

85
00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:27.051
"I believe this little fish escaped from an aquarium!"

86
00:04:29.793 --> 00:04:34.677
Dr. Dolittle and Tommy listened, recorded, and tried to speak to the fidgit all night.

87
00:04:35.778 --> 00:04:37.940
Yes, it had escaped from an aquarium.

88
00:04:38.881 --> 00:04:40.922
That's where it learned to speak human talk.

89
00:04:40.942 --> 00:04:45.106
"Tommy!" cried the doctor, sticking his head out of the tank.

90
00:04:45.606 --> 00:04:47.288
"The fidgit has something to say!"

91
00:04:48.828 --> 00:04:52.191
They both put their faces back into the water and waited.

92
00:04:52.211 --> 00:04:57.235
"Thank you for coming to see my show," the little fish began.

93
00:04:58.056 --> 00:05:01.519
Tommy started to giggle, which made bubbles under the water.

94
00:05:01.539 --> 00:05:03.720
"Please do not smoke.

95
00:05:04.221 --> 00:05:07.404
Do not tap on the glass," the fidgit continued.

96
00:05:07.424 --> 00:05:13.048
"And if you want to learn shellfish language, seek the great glass sea snail."

97
00:05:13.689 --> 00:05:15.931
"Er, who is that?"

98
00:05:16.491 --> 00:05:17.232
asked the doctor.

99
00:05:18.516 --> 00:05:22.420
"He is the oldest living creature in the world," the fidgit replied.

100
00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.564
"A snail that is as big as a house."

101
00:05:26.184 --> 00:05:27.386
"Where can we find him?"

102
00:05:28.126 --> 00:05:28.707
asked Tommy.

103
00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:33.051
"The snail lives only in one place," the fidgit answered.

104
00:05:33.071 --> 00:05:37.056
"Find Spider Monkey Island and you will find him."
